course: dictionary
lesson: 27
title: Formal words in context: abstain
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Abstain is a formal word. It means to choose not to do something, even though you could. «Sam decided to abstain from sweets during the whole of Lent.» Sam could eat sweets, but he chooses not to. The word from tells you what is being left out: sweets.
explain: In a vote, abstain means you choose not to vote yes or no. «141 countries voted yes, 5 voted no and 35 abstained, which means they chose not to vote yes or no, news reports said.» The clue is in the sentence: abstained is set against yes and no, so it must be a third choice.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase. If "chose not to" still makes sense in the sentence, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Abstain means to choose not to do something.
fact: Abstain is a formal word, often used in exams, in health and in voting.
fact: Abstain is usually followed by «from», as in «abstain from sugar».
fact: In a vote, to abstain means to choose not to vote yes or no.
fact: «Abstained» is the past tense, and «abstaining» is the -ing form.
exercise: «Priya will abstain from chocolate until her birthday.» What does abstain mean here? | Eat as much as she can | Buy lots of chocolate for her friends | *Choose not to eat it
exercise: «Thirty-five countries abstained in the vote.» What did these countries do? | Left the room for a snack | Voted yes | *Chose not to vote yes or no | Voted no
exercise: Mum says Dad will abstain from alcohol this month. Find and copy the verb that means choose not to do something. | alcohol | *abstain | month | Dad
test: «Lily will abstain from fizzy drinks for a month.» What does abstain mean? | Spill them on the floor | *Choose not to have them | Choose to have lots of them
test: In a class vote, Omar does not vote yes or no. Which word describes what Omar does? | *abstain | celebrate | explode
exam: Which sentence uses abstain correctly? | Ben abstained the cake on the table. | *Ben chose to abstain from cake while he was ill. | Ben abstained to the shop every day.
